      "previewImage": "previews/minimax-h3-10eros-beta6-t2v.jpg",
      "description": "TenStrip's 10Eros Max beta6 8-step TURBO (INT8, 21.7 GB) on the plain official graph: euler / simple, 10 steps, sigma shift 10 video / 3 audio, the settings from the author's notes and sampling example. The turbo is part of the checkpoint, so there is no LoRA node and no second file.\n\nThe author calls this a slow 8 to 12 step model, and the Steps control covers that range. He also warns that sparse attention destroys it, so this card offers Faster Attention only: no Sol-Attn, no Spectrum.\n\nOne-seed comparison against eight other H3 checkpoints (2026-10-09, RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB, 864x480, 15 s, engine v0.38.0): on a plain prose prompt for a three-beat scene it gave the strongest tilt and character reaction of the nine, and on a structured three-shot brief it cut at the scripted 5 and 10 second marks. The look leans to a sculpted, detailed stop-motion puppet. One seed and one scene, so treat this as a first impression; the audio was not judged by ear.\n\nFree system RAM matters more than VRAM; keep 16 GB+ free.\n\nVerified in SimpliGen 1.71.1 / engine v0.38.0 on a 12 GB RTX 4070 Ti: 15 s at 864x480, 10 steps, 418 s through the app, and the output matched the engine test frame for frame (same seed).",
